# Module hooks (LAW)

Canonical: `AIRULES/41-MODULE-HOOKS.md`. Sample: `AIRULES/examples/EX-16-module-hooks.md`.

- Name: **`module.{lowercase_modulename}.{hook_name}.hook`** (four lowercase segments; `hook_name` is `snake_case`).
- Fire **only** when another module could log, show history, or sync (SMS/mail sent, payment, lockout, finished workflow). **MUST NOT** fire on every save.
- Above `Events::trigger`: **MUST** `Hook:` / `Why:` / `About:` / `Params:` / `Use:` (if you cannot write `Use:`, do not fire).
- **MUST** document every fired name in `app/modules/<YourModule>/.hooks` (Markdown **content**, filename **`.hooks`**, module **root** — not `assets/`, not `hooks.md`).
- Same chunk: new trigger ↔ new `.hooks` heading. Stale rows **MUST** go.
- Payload: ids/counts/flags. **MUST NOT** passwords, OTP, tokens, rights, SMS/email bodies, request bodies.
- `trigger()` **ignores** listener returns — not a veto. Pre-action stop = **`triggerWithVeto()`** + `new \Dotsystems\App\Parts\Veto($code, $message, $details)` only. Ordinary `false`/scalar returns stay ignored. Never send `Veto` message/details to the browser.
- React to another module: **read its `.hooks`**, `Events::on` in **your** `module.listeners.php`. Cover the producer URL in `Listeners::initializeRoutes()` (omit/`null` inherits the module map). **MUST NOT** patch them or DACore.
- **MUST NOT** fire `dotapp.catchall` yourself. **MUST NOT** `trigger()` inside `foreach` of a growing list — one batch event.
- Finish gate: grep `Events::trigger(` vs `.hooks`; reject old `shop.item.saved` shape.
